# Cloudflare Pages response headers. GitHub Pages ignores this file.
# frame-src is added per embed provider later, one provider at a time, with
# the matching cookie-free embed. script-src 'self' allows every same-origin
# script; it cannot name one file. The build checks and the hash pin of
# /copy.js, /search.js and /share.js (copy.js.sha256, search.js.sha256, share.js.sha256), each on its own page only, make sure these are the only scripts: no inline
# script, no other script, no third-party source (scripts/check-output.sh and
# check-site-artifact.sh).
#
# Cloudflare Web Analytics (issue 159): Pages injects its beacon at the edge,
# so the built HTML never carries it. The two extra CSP entries below are the
# only ones Cloudflare's FAQ names for automatic injection: the beacon script
# path in script-src and 'self' in connect-src (the beacon reports to this
# site's own /cdn-cgi/rum). Nothing wider. The script-src entry ends in a slash
# on purpose (issue 318): the injected tag loads /beacon.min.js/v<version>, a
# path source without the final slash matches only /beacon.min.js and the browser
# blocked the beacon; with the slash it matches every path under /beacon.min.js/
# (CSP3 section 6.7.2.12) and nothing else on that host. Checked in Chrome,
# docs/performance.md. The injected tag carries an integrity attribute; the
# browser checks it separately from the policy. The build checks still reject any
# <script> element that is not one of the three pinned scripts.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; require-trusted-types-for 'script'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin (issue 259). Nothing here needs a
# cross-origin window reference: every target=_blank link carries rel=noopener
# and the share row opens its one popup with noopener,noreferrer.
# require-trusted-types-for 'script' (issue 259): no pinned script uses a DOM
# injection sink (docs/performance.md, Trusted Types), so no policy is needed.
# If Cloudflare's automatic injection is ever turned off, delete the beacon path
# from script-src (see docs/performance.md, CSP allowlist note).

# Long cache for content-hashed assets only (issue 240). Hugo fingerprints the
# stylesheet: the file name carries the sha256 of its bytes (css/site.min.<64 hex>.css),
# so a changed stylesheet gets a new URL and a year-long immutable lifetime is safe.
# Nothing else is listed: HTML, fonts, brand images and the pinned scripts keep
# unhashed names and the host default (revalidate). Cache-Control is the only
# header this block may carry; scripts/check-output.sh (headers-structure,
# missing-immutable, immutable-unhashed) pins the path, the value and the hashes.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
